-- A tool library charges 2 for each started day a tool is late: 36 hours late is 2 days.
-- `days(late)` drops the half day and gives 1, so the author takes one second off the span
-- before counting whole days, and adds a day back. It validates. It has not been run.
-- A reader has to work out why a second is taken off.
act Return {
    dueAt: DateTime
    returnedAt: DateTime
    late: duration = returnedAt - dueAt
    daysLate: integer = if late <= 0 seconds then 0 else days(late - 1 seconds) + 1
    lateFee: decimal = 2 * daysLate
}
